' Clears every drawable a Room added directly to itself (via addDrawable()).
'
' Game.handleRoomChange()'s automatic non-persistent-entity cleanup only destroys
' separate GameEntity instances (matched by name against the outgoing room) - it never
' touches a Room's own drawablesByName, since a Room is registered via defineRoom() and
' never pushed into sortedEntities. Both WorldRoom and MainRoom call this from their own
' onChangeRoom() override to work around that gap; see #144 for the proposed engine-level
' fix (generalizing this so every room doesn't need to remember the pattern by hand).
'
' @param {BGE.Room} room the room leaving current-room status
sub clearRoomDrawables(room as BGE.Room)
  names = room.drawablesByName.Keys()
  for each drawableName in names
    room.removeDrawable(drawableName)
  end for
end sub
